For a finite shift $\delta$, $\ket{\psi(t+\delta)}
=e^{-iH\delta}\ket{\psi(t)}.$ Expanding to first order, $\ket{\psi(t+\delta)}
=\left(\mathbf 1-i\delta H\right)\ket{\psi(t)}
+O(\delta^2).$ Thus $H$ is the infinitesimal generator that updates a state in time.

